[Music]  robert pattinson's performance in the  madman is a fascinating look at the  darkness that lurks inside the superhero  but there is one moment that exposes the  pain that bruce wayne suffers here is  the bruce wayne scene in the batman that  went too far fans of batman are well  aware that bruce wayne has a lot of  trauma to deal with especially when it  comes to his family as a young boy his  parents are both murdered leaving him an  orphan the tragic backstory is just a  part of what makes the characters so  rich and well-liked in matt reeves to  batman this aspect of bruce wayne is  still a crucial part of his story  because of what bruce goes through  growing up he desperately wants to stop  that from happening to anyone else and  to make gotham city a better place in  the new film fans get to see bruce  devoted to finding and stopping the  riddler and ridding the city of  corruption he works with james gordon  and selena kyle to get that job done in  the end bruce is a hero and it looks  like there is still some hope for gotham  to be better but even as a superhero  bruce certainly isn't perfect he's human  with issues that he has not fully dealt  with yet and this leads him to make some  bad decisions the batman highlights  these flaws alongside bruce's strengths  leading to one scene in the new film in  which bruce arguably takes a  conversation one step too far chances  are you already know that the man who  raises him after his parents deaths is  none other than his butler alfred  pennyworth alfred is a wonderful  parental figure and while bruce has some  things he definitely needs to work on he  turns out to be a pretty stand-up guy  but in the batman the riddler schemes  hit a little too close to home for bruce  causing him to question everything he  thinks he knows about his father thomas  wayne and in turn alfred in the first  half of the film bruce exhibits signs of  carelessness when it comes to his own  well-being sure he wears bulletproof  armor and can take care of himself in a  fight but he also takes unnecessary  risks and doesn't seem to care for much  outside of his vengeance with the new  mayoral candidate bella rael  highlighting the need for change on the  ground in gotham alfred brings up the  topic of the wayne legacy of  philanthropy to bruce alfred tells bruce  that the young man has no consideration  for maintaining the wayne family legacy  as upstanding citizens of gotham and  that's all bruce cares about as bringing  justice through batman he wants to  inflict his kind of justice  he's just compelled to do it he doesn't  even seem to give a second thought to  the idea of wayne's holdings and other  projects completely falling apart then  when alfred pushes once more bruce  responds emotionally snapping back at  alfred while bruce is likely pushing  alfred away to keep them both from  getting hurt he does more damage than he  thinks alfred's devotion and love for  the wayne family are probably the basis  of his identity and life audiences get a  deeper sense of this in the scene when  bruce is getting ready to attend the  mayor's funeral and alfred gives bruce  his wayne cufflinks to wear bruce  questions why alfred has them as he's  technically not a wane alfred reveals  that they were a cherished gift from  bruce's father bruce realizes that his  father giving alfred the cufflinks was a  declaration of alfred becoming a part of  the family bruce doesn't necessarily  apologize to alfred about the offense  and so many words but he realizes the  truth that alfred really is family after  the riddler's attempt on bruce's life  almost kills his devoted father figure  bruce stays by alfred's side in the  hospital as he recovers once he wakes up  the two have a very important  conversation about thomas and the things  bruce finds out about his father from  the riddler  look at this latest it's all about the  wings ultimately the scene builds to  them having a touching moment together  although bruce takes his anger and grief  a step too far in the earlier  conversation he thankfully comes to his  senses by the end of the batman and  makes it clear to alfred that they are  in fact family  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the batman are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]

